  "title": "Ordinal Numbers",
  "titleRussian": "Порядковые числительные",
  "description": "First, second, third and beyond",
  "descriptionRussian": "Первый, второй, третий и далее",
  "imageName": "list.number",
  "intro": "Ordinal numbers (first, second, third...) in Russian behave like adjectives - they agree in gender, number, and case with their noun! Most are formed regularly from cardinals, but the first few are irregular. Ordinals are used for dates, floors, chapters, and rankings. Remember: первый (1st), второй (2nd), третий (3rd) are unique forms you must memorize.",
  "rules": [
    "Ordinals behave exactly like adjectives — they agree in gender, number, AND case with their noun.",
    "Memorize the first three (первый, второй, третий) as they are completely irregular and cannot be derived from the cardinal.",
    "In compound numbers like 21st or 102nd, only the LAST word becomes ordinal: двадцать первый, сто второй.",
    "Ordinals are essential for dates (neuter form), floor numbers, and chapter references in everyday Russian."
  ],
  "examples": [
    "Первый этаж. (First floor.), masculine",
    "Вторая глава. (Second chapter.), feminine",
    "Третье место. (Third place.), neuter",
    "Двадцать первое января. (January 21st.), neuter for dates"
  ],
